    "text": {
     "en": "(additional, not in the textbook) We count bigger collections by making groups of ten.\nTen ones make one ten. Tie ten toys together as one bundle.\nIf you have 3 bundles and 4 loose toys, you have 34 toys.\nCounting in tens first and then ones is faster than counting one by one.\nAlways count the bundles first and then the loose ones."
    }
